      <p class="small muted">After a declared catastrophe the Commissioner may extend TWIA's deadlines (§2210.581). Always check the dates on your own TWIA letters.</p>

      <h2>Common reasons TWIA claims come up short</h2>
      <p>After every storm, a TWIA expert sees the same patterns in claim files that get denied or underpaid:</p>
      <ul class="checks xs">
        <li><strong>"Wear and tear" or "pre-existing."</strong> Older roofs still get damaged by wind. Creased shingles have lost their seal — that's storm damage, not age.</li>
        <li><strong>"Flood, not wind."</strong> Water marks, interior staining above flood lines, and missing roof components tell a different story.</li>
        <li><strong>Repair instead of replace.</strong> Spot repairs that can't match, or that don't meet the windstorm code TDI requires for a WPI-8, can leave you paying the difference.</li>
        <li><strong>Missing line items.</strong> Drip edge, starter, underlayment upgrades, permits, WPI-8 inspection costs and overhead and profit are routinely left out.</li>
        <li><strong>Missed deadlines and incomplete proof.</strong> TWIA decides on the information it has. We make sure it has everything.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>TWIA claims help after a denial or low offer</h2>
      <p>A denial letter isn't the end. Depending on why TWIA said no, we can supply new evidence and request a re-inspection, submit a supplemental claim for missed damage, invoke appraisal for amount disputes, or help you understand when a coverage dispute needs an attorney. The sooner we see your letter, the more options you keep.</p>

      <h2>Hiring a TWIA expert: what it costs</h2>
      <p>You pay nothing up front. Texas caps public adjuster fees at 10% of the settlement (Insurance Code §4102.104), your contract must be on a TDI-approved form, and you can rescind it in writing within 72 hours of signing. If the claim isn't paid, you owe nothing. Use our <a href="/calculators/#claim-calc">claim payout calculator</a> to see your net after deductible and fee.</p>

